+# Sync scope comes from the account's binding alone: the [sync] area keys are
+# removed, and binding, rebinding or joining a team changes what syncs with no
+# config edit
+
+Determination belongs to the account: unsigned or unbound = local; bound to a
+project of the account's personal team = personal; bound to a project of a team
+the account is a member of = team. The repo holds only the binding. *.local.*
+never leaves the machine.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. Card "the [sync] area keys are removed": satelle.toml accepts no per-area
+   [sync] scope key; loading one fails naming the key and the heal, and
+   satelle init removes them, proven by a config test and an init test.
+2. Card "determination belongs to the account": scope resolves from the
+   signed-in account and the explicit [sync] project binding only (none =
+   local, personal team = personal, member team = team, other team = local),
+   proven by a resolver test with a fake account service.
+3. Card "binding, rebinding or joining a team changes what syncs with no config
+   edit": satelle project bind, a rebind and a membership change each change
+   the scope satelle sync status reports on the next sync, proven by a CLI test.
+4. Card "*.local.* never leaves the machine": under every resolved scope,
+   proven by the .local exclusion tests iterating the three scopes.
+5. go build ./... and go test ./... pass.
